    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d979">

                <pb facs="1023" n="1011" xml:id="pg1011"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7490F/1–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-12T14:00:00-04:00">January 12, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>254. Department’s telegram no. 164 of January 8 which crossed your 247 of January
                    8, 4 p.m., represents the Department’s views on the question of a radio station
                    in Saudi Arabia and it will be appreciated therefore if you will obtain the
                    desired assurances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
